# sepolicy.rule — scoped to the daemon domain, never a broad permissive mode.
#
# Bench thermal mode (thermal.bench=true) disables thermal zones and zeroes
# cooling devices from the daemon. On-device denial that justified this rule:
#   root shell, u:r:magisk:s0: "can't create .../mode: Permission denied"
#   target label: u:object_r:sysfs_thermal:s0 (/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/mode
#   and cooling_device*/cur_state). Reads are already permitted; only write was
#   denied. The daemon also injects this rule live via `magiskpolicy --live`
#   so bench mode works without a reboot; this file carries it across reboots.
allow magisk sysfs_thermal file write
